stow-herbal-guide =    
    { "[head=1]" }Herbs, the Zone, and You[/head]
    { "[italic]" }Notes on local plants, field medicine, and other concoctions.[/italic]

    { "[head=2]" }Preparing Extracts[/head]
    Put your plants in a manual grinder, attach an empty beaker and select juice. Each plant listed here gives 10u of extract.

    { "[head=2]" }Field Medicine[/head]
    { "[bold]" }Bleeding:[/bold] Barberry, cloudberry or eyebright oil.
    { "[bold]" }Cuts and bruises:[/bold] Gooseberry or calamus oil.
    { "[bold]" }Puncture wounds:[/bold] White cinquefoil oil.
    { "[bold]" }Burns:[/bold] Cranberry or sea buckthorn oil. For heat burns, not acid or electrical injuries.
    { "[bold]" }Radiation:[/bold] Raspberry or linden oil.
    { "[bold]" }Poison damage:[/bold] Goji, irga or spotted orchid oil.

    { "[head=2]" }Medicine Recipes[/head]
    { "[bold]" }Brute mixture[/bold]
    1u calamus oil + 1u white cinquefoil oil + 1u gooseberry oil.
    Makes 3u. Treats cuts, bruises and puncture wounds.

    { "[bold]" }Caustic mixture[/bold]
    2u cranberry oil + 1u irga oil.
    Makes 3u. Treats heat burns and toxin damage.

    { "[head=2]" }Hunting Mixtures[/head]
    { "[bold]" }Butcher's Bile[/bold]
    A cheap hunting poison developed specifically to handle mutant wildlife.
    5u wolfberry extract + 5u barberry oil.
    Makes 10u, enough for five bolts.

    { "[bold]" }Black Oil[/bold]
    A potent poison that resembles black tar. It'll pack a punch against even the toughest mutants.
    5u Butcher's Bile + 5u baneberry extract.
    Makes 5u, enough for two bolts with 1u left over.